@convince_lvp_eckener
view-if: lvp_formed
max-visits: 1
go-to: convince_lvp_success_eckener if ((lvp_relation >= 50 and lvp_ideology == "Right") or (lvp_relation >= 40 and lvp_ideology == "Moderate") or (lvp_relation >= 30 and lvp_ideology == "Left")) and (lvp_leader != "Coalfax" or lvp_ideology != "Right"); convince_lvp_fail_eckener if not (((lvp_relation >= 50 and lvp_ideology == "Right") or (lvp_relation >= 40 and lvp_ideology == "Moderate") or (lvp_relation >= 30 and lvp_ideology == "Left")) and (lvp_leader != "Coalfax" or lvp_ideology != "Right"))

The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> vote has been falling over time, especially during the current economic depression, so they will probably be of minimal help to us. Still, every little bit counts. They will certainly be a hard party to convince, with vehemently anti-<span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> industrialists influencing the party away from Eckhart.

@convince_lvp_success_eckener
on-arrival: lvp_support_marcher = 1; lvp_left += 3; lvp_relation += 4; guild_lvp -= 2; landed_lvp -= 2; guild_kvp += 2; landed_kvp += 2; guild_kvp += 2 if not kvp_formed; landed_kvp += 2 if not kvp_formed
go-to: endorsements_eckener

We have convinced the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> to give Eckhart an official endorsement, to the displeasure of the party's industrial backers. In response, they begin to withdraw their support from the party, and a notable portion of right-wing voters are opting to abstain.

@convince_lvp_fail_eckener
on-arrival: lvp_support_marcher = 0; lvp_right += 3; lvp_relation -= 5
go-to: endorsements_eckener

We have failed to persuade the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> to back <span style="color: #c00000;">Bristol</span>, due to their deep antipathy toward cooperating with the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>—even with Eckhart at the head of the ticket. This is a major blow—Eckhart was meant to be a unity candidate, and we've clearly failed in that objective.

@convince_z_eckener
choose-if: marcher_votes >= unionist_votes and not concord_formed
unavailable-subtitle: [? if marcher_votes < unionist_votes: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate. ?][? if concord_formed: The <span style="color: #000000;">Concord</span> can never be convinced. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.unionist_support_marcher = 0;
if (Q.unionist_relation >= 45 || (Q.unionist_relation > 35 && Q.unionist_ideology == "Left")) {
    Q.unionist_support_marcher = 1;
} else if (Q.unionist_relation >= 30) {
    Q.unionist_support_marcher = 2;
} else {
    Q.unionist_support_marcher = 0;
}
if (Q.unionist_relation >= 65) Q.bvp_support_marcher = 1;
!}
go-to: z_failed_eckener if unionist_support_marcher = 0; z_success_eckener if unionist_support_marcher = 1; z_partial_eckener if unionist_support_marcher = 2
max-visits: 1

We remind the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> of our past friendships, our support of Wilhelm Croft in 4290, and promote Eckhart as a non-partisan unity candidate that can stop the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>.

@z_success_eckener
go-to: endorsements_eckener

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is convinced! They will be part of the Eckhart coalition. [? if bvp_support_marcher: The <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> has also, surprisingly, joined the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] in endorsing Eckhart. ?][? if not bvp_support_marcher: However, the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> has split from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and refuses to back Eckhart. ?]

@z_failed_eckener
go-to: endorsements_eckener

Unfortunately, we are unable to convince the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> for some reason. 

@z_partial_eckener

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is not satisfied with our arguments, but they are open to being convinced if we front the resources.

- @pay_z_eckener: Give them the resources they need.
- @endorsements_braun: Forget about the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].

@pay_z_eckener
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources
on-arrival: resources -= 1; unionist_support_marcher = 1; bvp_support_marcher = 1 if unionist_relation >= 65
go-to: endorsements_eckener

With our resources, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] are convinced to support Eckhart. [? if bvp_support_marcher: The <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> has also, surprisingly, joined the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] in endorsing Eckhart. ?][? if not bvp_support_marcher: However, the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> has split from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and refuses to back Eckhart. ?]

@convince_dvp_eckener
view-if: not lvp_formed and gold_exist
max-visits: 1
go-to: convince_dvp_success_eckener if (gold_relation >= 70 and gold_ideology == "Right") or (gold_relation >= 60 and gold_ideology == "Moderate") or (gold_relation >= 50 and gold_ideology == "Left"); convince_dvp_fail_eckener if not ((gold_relation >= 70 and gold_ideology == "Right") or (gold_relation >= 60 and gold_ideology == "Moderate") or (gold_relation >= 50 and gold_ideology == "Left"))

The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> will be the most difficult of the propertied parties to convince, given their preference to keep their distance from us. However, Eckhart’s status as a non-partisan conservative presents a unique opportunity to win them over.

@convince_dvp_success_eckener
on-arrival: gold_support_marcher = 1; gold_left += 3; gold_relation += 5
go-to: endorsements_eckener

Thanks to our friendly relations and Eckhart's non-partisanship, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is now campaigning for Eckhart in the election. However, they refuse to join <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span>-led campaign committees and emphasize their independence from us.

@convince_dvp_fail_eckener
on-arrival: gold_support_marcher = 0; gold_right += 1; gold_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements_eckener

Unfortunately, under the influence of their industrialist wing, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> has rejected our overtures and will continue on their own path.